"""Serialize human-read adjudications; no heading/keyword-generated verdicts."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,csv,datetime
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
items=[]; entries=[]
PK='MPL_14_087-132'
def add(n,ns,kind,scans,lines,words,statement,recon,check,reason,verdict='kept'):
    src=[f'{PK}#{i}' for i in ns]
    ident=f'SA06-{n}'
    items.append(dict(id=ident,sources=src,kind=kind,cote=14,scans=scans,lines=[f'pro/{PK}_transcription.tex:{lines}'],his_words=words,statement=statement,reconstruction=recon,check=check,check_reason=reason))
    for j,s in enumerate(src):entries.append(dict(entry_id=s,item_id=ident,verdict=verdict if j==0 or verdict!='kept' else 'merged',reason=reason if j==0 or verdict!='kept' else 'Same object/claim as '+src[0]+'. '+reason))
add(200,[1],'unpursued implication',[87,89],'5-37;72-88','application ``graphe'' (pas additive!)','For abelian varieties A,B, u↦[Γu] in the full Chow/cohomology ring of A×B is not additive; its H^1-correspondence component is additive.','The separation into Künneth components is the earlier run’s explanation; the nonadditivity warning is explicit.','agrees','The graph is explicitly labelled nonadditive on scan87; scan89 extracts the mixed H^1⊗H^1 component. No anabelian assertion occurs.')
add(201,[2],'self-flagged step',[89],'72-88','Question Prouver ... soit algébrique','For abelian varieties over an algebraically closed field, divisor classes on A×B modulo pullbacks from the factors correspond to Hom(A,B∨), with the precise cycle-equivalence convention required. The proposed criterion for algebraicity of a mixed H^1 class is unfinished.','Using Pic/NS and a normalized Poincaré line bundle gives a precise modern formulation; no arithmetic field or invariant-class criterion is supplied.','agrees','The quotient and Hom identification are written; the last sentence stops before its condition. It cannot be called a stated Tate or anabelian theorem.')
add(202,[3],'reading question',[87],'7-12;25-35','H^1(A)×H^1(A*)→Qℓ(+1|-1)','The Poincaré pairing on first cohomology of dual abelian varieties is valued in Qℓ(-1), whereas the Tate-module Weil pairing is valued in Qℓ(1).','The sign is a type/weight check by this run, not a decision on ink.','agrees','The ambiguous twist is real and changes the duality type; retaining the ambiguity is correct.')
add(203,[4],'conjecture',[92],'130-177','groupe libre de type fini?; Groupe fini?; V.A.?','The diagram asks separately for finite generation/freeness of discrete cycle quotients, finiteness of a difference of equivalence relations, and representability of a continuous part by an abelian variety.','The braces do not fix every kernel/quotient unambiguously; modern notation must not erase these questions.','agrees','Question marks qualify distinct rows; none is proved by the chart.')
add(204,[5],'reading question',[92],'160-177','A_{Qℓ-hom}; A_{Zℓ-hom}','The chart proposes comparisons between cycle equivalences and rational/integral ℓ-adic homology, alongside K-theoretic and Picard/Albanese levels; several arrows are queried or cancelled.','The entry’s reference to Qℓ/Zℓ is not an exact transcription of the visible two separately labelled homological rows.','overstates','The page has Qℓ and Zℓ-labelled rows, not a plainly written Qℓ/Zℓ quotient; no comparison theorem can be extracted from crossed arrows.','corrected')
add(205,[6],'unproved claim',[88,79,82,84],'44-69; codex/K14-06:244-279,357-385,436-468','La notion de faisceau C-acyclique n’est pas intrinsèque','For a ringed topos (E,A), H^q(S,F)=0 for every S∈E and q>0 is equivalent to vanishing of Čech cohomology for every epimorphic covering family; site-specific acyclicity restricts the objects tested.','The missing continuation in the Pro package is supplied by Codex scan79, not reconstructed.','understates','Scan88 starts Proposition3.4; K14-06scan79 contains condition(ii), both implications and Definition3.5. The earlier note’s off-page limitation is removed in this combined packet.','corrected')
add(206,[7],'unproved claim',[90,77,86],'95-120; codex/K14-06:131-170,494-529','Les morphismes ... sont des isomorphismes lorsque q égale 0 ou 1','The Čech-to-derived comparison is an isomorphism for q≤n and injective for q=n+1 when the positive cohomology presheaves below n vanish; local effacement kills Čech H^0 of higher cohomology presheaves.','The exact site hypotheses are those of the surrounding SGA4 redaction; this is a comparison on refinements, not a bare arbitrary spectral-sequence claim.','understates','K14-06scan77 explicitly supplies the vanishing of Čech H^0(H^q), q≠0, that the note calls a missing ingredient.','corrected')
add(207,[8],'unproved claim',[97],'331-344','B̂ est isomorphe ... à B̂′','The editorial proposal relates formal smoothness to an isomorphism with a completed symmetric algebra on a projective module, in a topology and setup inherited from absent preceding numbered statements.','No full hypothesis set is recoverable from this sheet; do not substitute the unrestricted false assertion that every formally smooth algebra is a polynomial algebra.','agrees','The cited 2.2/3.3/3.4 and their hypotheses are not printed continuously here.')
add(208,[9],'reading question',[97],'340-344','A contient un corps','For a complete Noetherian local ring A, containing a field is equivalent to being a quotient of k[[T1,…,Tr]] for a coefficient field k; if char κ(A)=p>0, this is equivalent to pA=0.','The relation p>0 and power-series brackets are mathematical reconstructions only.','agrees','The transcription leaves a blank relation and missing brackets; Cohen’s theorem identifies the intended kind of assertion but does not identify ink.')
add(209,[10,11],'reading question',[99],'375-387','v1:A ... E; ... ensemble principal homogène','Given a square-zero extension E→C of A-algebras, kernel J, and u:B→C, the set of A-algebra lifts B→E is empty or a torsor under Der_A(B,J).','Replace the displayed domain A of v1 by B only in the separately labelled modern statement; frozen text remains unchanged.','misreads','The written v1-domain is incompatible with pv1=u. After correcting that domain, subtracting two lifts and expanding products proves the torsor statement; the run’s proof is sound.','rests on a misreading')
add(210,[12],'withdrawn in the same text',[101],'455-461','La démonstration de lemme B est immédiate','Lemma C(a) asserts existence of compatible maps between truncated algebras and truncated symmetric algebras with associated-graded surjectivity; C(b) is struck out while unfinished.','The absent lemmas A,B and undefined inverse-system setup prevent a complete theorem identification.','agrees','The quantifier edits in (a), inconsistent w-index, and total cancellation of (b) are visible; a single truncation is insufficient.')
add(211,[13],'unproved claim',[104],'513-534','e+codim_Y{y}≥trdeg_{κ(y)}κ(x)+codim_X{x}','For an irreducible finite-type dominant morphism X→Y with Y locally Noetherian, the displayed dimension inequality holds; equality holds when O_Y,y is a quotient of a regular local ring. For x closed in its fibre the residue transcendence term vanishes.','Universal catenarity is a modern sufficient condition explaining the equality clause.','agrees','The inequality direction and equality hypothesis are explicit; the margin requests reformulation, not reversal.')
add(212,[14],'withdrawn in the same text',[114],'818-836','cd U≤dim A','The cancelled draft claims an étale cohomological-dimension bound for a principal open in a complete local ring and attempts reduction to a finite extension of a power-series ring over a field.','Coefficient, residue-field and equal-characteristic assumptions must be stated separately; Codex reads égales car|car.|dim where Pro gives égale dim.','agrees','The whole attempted proof is deleted. Under only the literal printed hypotheses the bound fails, e.g. R[[t]][1/t]=R((t)) has infinite 2-cohomological dimension; this is a mathematical test, not a correction of ink.')
add(213,[15,16],'self-flagged step',[122,124],'1028-1045;1057-1088','M_v ... g^{-1}v∈W; n⊂m_a','For a group scheme G acting on V and a closed W with normalizer N, the incidence space is G×^N W when the fpqc quotient exists; its fibre is the transporter of v into W. Tangent inequalities alone do not imply smoothness.','Hypotheses include representability, N flat and quasi-compact, and G/N representable; both selected typescript leaves are cancelled.','agrees','Typed pagination puts124(p2) before122(p3); two unattached question marks do not identify one failed formula.')
add(214,[17,18],'unproved claim',[127,129],'1132-1147;1230-1237','Conserver le texte ci-contre, barré par erreur','Regular elements of a smooth group lie in a unique Cartan subgroup in the stated SGA3 setup; the regular incidence map identifies a dense open. A torus over any field is unirational via Weil restriction from a finite separable splitting field and the norm.','The full base hypotheses are supplied by the printed SGA3 theorem, not by the detached page; the norm proof proves unirationality, not rationality.','agrees','The restored cancellation at127 must not be recorded as a mathematical retraction; the printed parallel is SGA3 XIII §3.')
add(215,[19],'reading question',[132],'1301-1305','x²|x³−y²; k[x,y]/xy','These are isolated candidate ring/singularity fragments without a proposition, assumptions or asserted relation.','A normalization or singular-curve interpretation is only an earlier-run lead.','agrees','No complete mathematical assertion can be attributed to these fragments.')
add(216,[20],'unproved claim',[94,95],'191-242','χ(F⊗L^{⊗n})→+∞','For a projective scheme X over a field and invertible L, ampleness is equivalent to divergence of χ(Z,L^n|Z) for every positive-dimensional integral closed Z; the coherent-sheaf version is equivalent.','Modern formulations may assume merely proper X; that extension is a literature result, not already proved by the sheet.','agrees','The projectivity and all-positive-dimensional-subscheme quantifier are explicit; no novelty claim follows from a previous register label.')
add(217,[21],'idea of the earlier run',[94],'204-218','χ(L^{⊗n}⊗O_Z)≥2','Over k=R, X=P¹_C as an integral projective R-scheme with L=O_X has χ_R=h⁰_R=2 for every power but L is not ample. Thus the finite threshold conditions as literally quantified over k need a geometric constants convention.','This counterexample is the earlier run’s construction, independently checked here; it is not on Grothendieck’s page.','agrees','The page says only corps k, and its finite thresholds do not impose geometric integrality or k-valued constants. χ-growth remains unaffected.')
add(218,[22],'withdrawn in the same text',[94,95],'229-276','cf lettre de Mumford; supprimer ... section ... projectif?','The two induction lemmas concern eventual H^i(X,L^n)=0 for i≥2 under ample restrictions and eventual basepoint-freeness given a nonzero section; questions ask whether section existence/projectivity can be dropped in cancelled variants.','A nonzero section and the dimension≥2 induction context are necessary qualifications; proper-scheme Nakai does not validate every cancelled finite-threshold variant.','agrees','d,d′ are deleted on94 and the two lemmas refer externally to Mumford. The live questions persist, with that provenance.')
add(219,[23],'conjecture',[96],'295-328','xP>0 ?⇒ x∈R','On a smooth projective surface, does positivity of D·C for every integral curve imply ampleness? The missing condition is D²>0. Strictly nef square-zero divisors supply negative examples.','P must mean actual effective curve classes rather than every nonzero limiting class of the closed cone for this counterexample.','agrees','The text itself reduces its question to excluding square zero.')
add(220,[24],'idea of the earlier run',[94],'220-227','D.C>0; D^d>0','The curve-and-top-intersection test does not imply ampleness in dimension3: on V=P_S(O⊕H), D=ξ+π*L with L strictly nef, L²=0 and H very ample, D·C>0 for every curve and D³=H²+3HL>0, but D² on the quotient section is zero.','Projective bundle is in quotient convention; the explicit construction belongs to the earlier run and is checked here.','agrees','The marginal criterion omits intermediate-dimensional subvarieties; the construction meets the stated projective hypotheses.')
add(221,[25],'unpursued implication',[96,98,100],'322-328;355-362;390-430','Question; P_i^{+0}.P_{d−i}^{+0}≥0 ?','The 31 August1964 letter to Mumford asks closely parallel strict-positivity and higher-cycle cone-product questions.','This establishes a textual parallel, not a date for the undated Montpellier leaves.','agrees','The two endpoints concern the same questions but use different cone labels; the correspondence is checked separately in links.')
add(222,[26],'idea of the earlier run',[100],'390-430','D.C≥0 ... D^d≥0 ??','For a nef Cartier divisor D on a smooth projective d-fold, D^r·Z≥0 for every integral r-dimensional subvariety Z, including D^d≥0; approximate D by D+εH with H ample.','The approximation argument is the earlier run’s modern proof; general higher-codimension classes are excluded.','agrees','The initial question concerns powers of a divisor, and the cubic expansion is compatible with this proof.')
add(223,[27],'conjecture',[98,100],'355-362;406-410','α_i(P_i^{+0})⊂P_{d−i}^+','Under numerical Poincaré duality, must a nef higher-codimension class be pseudoeffective, and must products of complementary nef classes be nonnegative? These assertions fail on suitable powers of a CM elliptic curve.','Identification of every draft α_i with the numerical duality map is conditional; the precise modern cone statement is separated.','agrees','The boxed complementary-product and cone-duality questions are present and are stronger than the divisor case.')
add(224,[28],'reading question',[96],'328','χ(O(nD))=χ(X)+nχ(D)','For D²=0 on a smooth surface, Riemann–Roch gives χ(O(nD))=χ(O_X)−n(D·K_X)/2. If higher cohomology vanishes eventually, h⁰≥χ; the manuscript’s χ(D) must denote its linear coefficient before interpreting its sign.','The coefficient interpretation is a reconstruction; χ(D) is not silently equated with χ(O_D).','agrees','The final <|≤ ambiguity and absent local χ(D) definition prevent the last sign conclusion from being securely read.')
add(225,[29],'unproved claim',[103],'476-502','K∩J¹(X) fini, donc K de type fini','For a smooth projective surface X and smooth hyperplane curve Y, the kernel K of Pic(X)→Pic(Y) is finitely generated when its intersection with Pic⁰(X) is finite, because its image in NS(X) is finitely generated. Restriction NS(X)→NS(Y) has finite cokernel and rank-ρ−1 kernel.','Identify J¹ with Pic⁰ and the discrete quotient using scan117; the lower M|N symbol stays uncertain.','agrees','The finite-intersection argument needs the Néron–Severi theorem; it does not apply to arbitrary higher J^i.')
add(226,[30],'self-flagged step',[103],'500-504','Je présume ... courbes irréductibles','The proposed generic finiteness of the Picard restriction kernel is linked to irreducible limiting members in a pencil.','The precise meaning of en général, the pencil and exceptional characteristics is not fixed sufficiently for a universal theorem.','agrees','The preceding kernel question is cancelled; the final presumption remains live and conditional.')
add(227,[31],'conjecture',[106,107,108,109],'539-687','Conjectures Lefschetz locales','Let S=Spec A for a strictly local Noetherian ring, X its punctured spectrum, Y=X∩V(f), U=X−Y, with X,Y regular. The page predicts vanishing/finite-error ranges and restriction properties of its A,J,N cycle groups governed by an undefined N.','N=dim A is plausible but not stated; A,J,N outside the proper setting and finite versus p-primary errors need separate definitions.','agrees','No theorem follows without defining those objects; the Pro/Codex ≥|= disagreement in the first range is retained.')
add(228,[32],'unproved claim',[107],'588-605','conséquence de 1° et 2°','Conditional on the preceding local vanishing and restriction assertions and cycle localization, the map A^i(X)→A^i(U) is predicted to be an isomorphism modulo finite groups, with a stronger integral range, and the Gysin map from Y is zero in specified ranges.','For Chow groups, a principal divisor and the projection formula make Gysin zero when its classes lift from X; this is a conditional derivation.','agrees','The manuscript gives no standalone exact-sequence proof and does not license discarding finite or p-primary qualifications.')
