add(230,[34,36],'self-flagged step',[108,109],'645-687','définir un complémentaire naturel; Donner un sens','Define natural complements and a monodromy action making J¹(X)=J¹(Y)^π (N=3) and N¹(X)=N¹(Y)^π (N=4) meaningful; the next lines request the odd/even critical-degree cycle vanishings.','Cohomological fixed-part theorems and isogeny-category complements are weaker than a canonical integral cycle-group splitting.','agrees','Neither π nor the category of the complement is defined; the congruence notation retains finite-group error.')
add(231,[35],'idea of the earlier run',[108,117],'660-664;938-947','J¹ ... bij; N¹ ... inj; ⇒ A¹ ... bij','A map of short exact sequences with isomorphism on J and injection on N yields injection on A, not surjection without another premise.','A simple split-group countermodel checks the inference only; it does not by itself refute a geometrically strengthened theorem.','agrees','The last bijective label is unsupported by the two displayed premises and is a scan-review alarm.')
add(232,[37],'conjecture',[111,112],'690-747','A_r ... rationnelle','For smooth projective X^n and a smooth hyperplane Y over the written closed field, the manuscript predicts Chow restriction and Gysin isomorphisms in weak-Lefschetz-looking ranges, with separate τ-subgroup and algebraic-equivalence refinements.','This is about rational equivalence, not merely cycle classes in cohomology; separably versus algebraically closed is a Pro/Codex conflict.','agrees','The erased alg and inserted rationnelle are decisive; all exceptional-characteristic qualifiers remain.')
add(233,[38],'withdrawn in the same text',[112],'749-767','injectif exc. p → bijectif mod groupes finis','The live revision asks L^(n−2i):A_a^i→A_a^(n−i) to be an isomorphism modulo finite groups and L^(n−2i+1) on the τ-subgroup of rational Chow classes to have the analogous property.','A_a is modulo algebraic equivalence, hence this exceeds the standard algebraic hard-Lefschetz conjecture on cohomology classes.','agrees','The source subgroup/quotient and injective/bijective amendments change the statement and cannot be erased.')
add(234,[39],'idea of the earlier run',[111,112],'695-697;763-767','surjectif mod grp finis si p≥n−2i+1','At n=2,i=1,p=1, the unconditional whole-Chow assertion predicts CH¹(X)→CH₀(X) with finite cokernel. For a complex projective K3 surface the divisor-product image is cyclic whereas the degree-zero Chow group is infinite-dimensional; the assertion fails.','Use a smooth projective quartic K3 in characteristic0 and an ample hyperplane class; this tests no uncertain τ notation.','agrees','All of the written hypotheses and indices specialize; the counterexample concerns the concluding unconditional map, not a cohomological Lefschetz theorem.')
add(235,[40],'reading question',[113],'771-804','A_r^i(X)/Im A_r^i(Y); dim 2n+1','For a smooth divisor Y⊂X, CH^(i−1)(Y)→CH^i(X)→CH^i(X−Y)→0 is the localization sequence. For E=L× over an n-fold, dim E=n+1 and CH^i(E)=coker(c1(L):CH^(i−1)(X)→CH^i(X)).','The ordinary punctured cone interpretation and corrected indices are explicitly a reconstruction.','misreads','The transcribed same-codimension localization and 2n+1 conflict with their declared geometry; both Pro and Codex retain them, so ink review is necessary.','rests on a misreading')
