add(244,[49],'idea of the earlier run',[126,128],'1111-1124;1178-1185','x↦(x)−(0) est un hom','For an abelian variety A over an algebraically closed field, δ(x)=[x]−[0] is a set section of alb:CH₀(A)^0→A(k); it is a group homomorphism exactly when [x+y]−[x]−[y]+[0]=0 rationally. If additive, it is surjective and hence inverse to alb.','This conditional group argument is independently checked; it does not assert additivity for all A.','agrees','The manuscript’s hom label is the decisive unproved premise; two abstract surjections do not imply an isomorphism.')
