add(248,[53,54],'unproved claim',[120],'980-1008','Conditions équivalentes; ... F+R','For a projective scheme X, bounded families of differences of vector-bundle classes admit a common sufficiently negative free quotient presentation and finitely many Hilbert polynomials; replacing G by a kernel R gives ξ+[O(-n)^N]=[F⊕R].','Uniform boundedness of kernels supplies a possibly different twist; no fixed old n is asserted by the completed proof.','agrees','The inserted finite-polynomial requirement matters and the last sentence stops before the common quotient is named.')
add(249,[55,56],'withdrawn in the same text',[121,123],'1011-1024;1048-1053','Conditions [équivalentes]; (ii)⇒(i)⇔(iv)⇒(iii)⇒(v)','The live cycle-boundedness result is only the displayed implication chain, with a fixed translate making representatives effective, a bounded K-family and the factor (i−1)! in the Chern-class relation.','K-equivalence is not defined in this fragment, so rational-Chow counterexamples do not automatically refute the exact draft statement.','agrees','The equivalence heading is deleted and the later arrows do not contain the missing converses; factorials cannot be cancelled integrally.')
