add(251,[58],'unproved claim',[131],'1242-1284','A(Y(y))=Im A(X)+Im A(C)','The generic-fibre blowup calculation seeks to generate cycles on Y over k(S) by restrictions from X and exceptional-centre cycles, using extension by closure, a blowup formula and identification of the exceptional family over a rational base.','Requires smooth blowup geometry, the stated trivialization and rational-Chow/base-change hypotheses; not automatically true over an algebraic closure of k(S).','agrees','u_y=u and the final codimension/summation notation are the unsupported steps; y′ after restriction is a type alarm.')
