add(254,[61],'idea of the earlier run',[112,117],'750-767;928-950','E; partie primitive','On a Lefschetz string v_a=L^a v_0 of length r, inverse lowering has coefficient1, whereas an sl₂ lowering satisfying [e,f]=h with hv_a=(2a−r)v_a has coefficient a(r−a+1).','The normalized comparison is an earlier-run computation, independently recomputed; it is not an identified formula in this range.','not on the page','Primitive notation does not determine a lowering normalization.')
add(255,[62],'idea of the earlier run',[87,117],'5-35;928-950','H¹; partie primitive','In the Tate category generated by h(P¹)=1⊕Q(-1), tensor automorphisms fix the unit inclusion, whereas nonzero Lefschetz raising does not. Therefore its sl₂ action is not automatically a subgroup action of that motivic Galois group.','Counterexample addresses the earlier-run proposed inclusion only; Grothendieck makes no such inclusion here.','not on the page','The page supplies twists/cycle notation but no comparison of these symmetry groups.')
add(256,[63],'idea of the earlier run',[87,117],'7-12;928-950','Qℓ(1)','A tensor weight cocharacter and the variety-dependent shifted Lefschetz Cartan grading are different structures; the latter acts on H⁰(P¹) with nonzero shifted weight.','This is an earlier-run conceptual test, not a text reconstruction.','not on the page','No weight cocharacter is defined in these pages.')
add(257,[64],'idea of the earlier run',[87,89],'7-12;79-85','H¹(A)⊗H¹(B)(1)','For a morphism L:h^i(X)→h^(i+2)(X)(1), naturality gives g_(i+2)Lg_i^(-1)=χ(g)^(-1)L after trivializing the Tate line; it commutes with kerχ.','The tensor-automorphism computation is the earlier run’s, not an assertion on the selected sheets.','not on the page','The twists motivate the test; the motivic-group formula is absent.')
add(258,[65],'reading question',[111,117],'690-950','Conjectures Lefschetz','The current range has no definitions of standard-conjecture letters A–D; assignments proposed from absent cote16 must remain external and unequal in certainty.','Printed A/B/C/D conventions cannot be substituted for these stronger Chow-group assertions.','agrees','The bounded absence is confirmed by reading the entire range; no manuscript letter concordance is established here.')
add(259,[66],'idea of the earlier run',[112],'750-767','bijectif mod groupes finis','Universal standard-conjecture equivalences quantified over varieties/products differ from an implication for one fixed X; the sheet’s cycle-group maps are finer still.','The A(k)=C(k) statement is an earlier-run report of absent cote16.','not on the page','No field-quantified conjecture equivalence occurs on112.')
add(260,[67],'unpursued implication',[117],'938-947','N*=A_a*','Numerical motives are semisimple over characteristic-zero coefficients, whereas this N denotes cycles modulo algebraic equivalence. Nilpotence of a comparison kernel is not its vanishing.','Jannsen’s results are later comparisons; they do not decide the page’s finer quotient.','agrees','The notation check is decisive and the semisimplicity assertion is not attributed to the page.')
add(261,[68],'unpursued implication',[112],'750-767','E^(n−2i)','Motivic Lefschetz decompositions for abelian schemes and the Beauville grading involve rational coefficients and a shifted exponent g−2p+s on CH_s^p; they do not imply whole-Chow surjectivity at the unshifted exponent.','The abelian-motive comparison is external.','agrees','The earlier run retains the different coefficient and eigenspace hypotheses.')
add(262,[69],'idea of the earlier run',[112,113],'753-803','mod groupes finis','A map with finite kernel/cokernel is a rational isomorphism, but 0→Q/Z is a rational isomorphism with infinite cokernel; separate torsion control is necessary for the converse.','This elementary countermodel is the earlier run’s, independently checked.','agrees','The manuscript’s repeated finite-group qualification cannot be replaced by rational equivalence of maps.')
add(263,[70],'unpursued implication',[108,109,111,112],'645-678;690-767','Donner un sens à la formule','Hard Lefschetz and global invariant cycles in ℓ-adic cohomology do not supply algebraic inverse correspondences, integral Chow finite-error bounds or canonical local cycle complements.','Deligne’s theorem is external and matches only the cohomological comparison.','agrees','The note correctly limits what the literature can establish for the stronger manuscript statements.')
add(264,[71],'unpursued implication',[106,107,113,114],'539-612;771-836','Conjectures Lefschetz locales','The pages propose local punctured-space and vanishing-cycle questions while retaining regular X,Y; the cone and cancelled cd argument do not construct a singular correspondence formalism.','The link to absent cote16’s singular-hypersurface programme is thematic.','agrees','The note does not silently remove smoothness or turn cancelled material into a proof.')
add(265,[72],'idea of the earlier run',[107],'607-611','Définir des formes','A complex nodal rational cubic has one-dimensional rational H¹; its degree-one alternating intersection pairing cannot be nondegenerate. Singular generalizations need a replacement for ordinary Poincaré duality.','This is an earlier-run example, independently checked topologically; no particular replacement is attributed to Grothendieck.','not on the page','The sheet asks for forms but contains no nodal-cubic calculation.')
add(266,[75],'idea of the earlier run',[87,89],'5-12;72-88','Hom(A,B*)','The earlier run compares Tate/Faltings Hom theorems for abelian varieties with anabelian Hom theorems for hyperbolic curves, under distinct field, openness and quotient hypotheses.','These are external project comparisons; the truncated algebraicity question supplies no such theorem.','not on the page','No arithmetic base field, fundamental group or section map is defined in this range.')
add(267,[76],'idea of the earlier run',[92,117],'130-177;928-950','V.A.?','Reductivity/semisimple representations do not imply trivial centre (G_m); a centre-free profinite kernel gives a separate outer-action reconstruction of extensions.','The profinite comparison belongs to earlier-run project context.','not on the page','Neither slimness nor the arithmetic extension reconstruction is stated in this range.')
add(268,[77],'idea of the earlier run',[87,92],'5-35;130-177','V.A.?','Polarizability and real descent are distinct: a polarization does not furnish the semilinear involution needed for descent from C to R.','The compact-real-form criterion cited by the earlier run is a later Tannakian comparison, not a manuscript conclusion.','not on the page','The selected pages do not assert this bridge.')
add(269,[78],'idea of the earlier run',[87,89],'7-12;79-85','Qℓ(1)','For a cusp in characteristic0, Kummer inertia conjugation is cyclotomic. This forward calculation supplies no converse recognizing arbitrary procyclic subgroups, and differs from a weight cocharacter G_m→G.','The Kummer calculation is earlier-run work, independently checked algebraically; outside the manuscript topic.','not on the page','No cusp or normalizer criterion is stated here.')
add(270,[79],'reading question',[129],'1230','si N est le normalisateur','The normalizer in this reused sheet is a Cartan-subgroup normalizer in an algebraic group, not the procyclic normalizer from anabelian projects.','Unavailable LM6 A.50 and A.22 remain earlier-run leads; truncated statements cannot be reconstructed.','agrees','The local G/N context identifies the normalizer type directly.')
add(271,[80],'idea of the earlier run',list(range(87,133)),'1-1312','','No motivic Galois exact sequence appears in this selected range; the earlier run supplies a modern Nori exact sequence as a separate comparison.','Do not interpret it as a rational-point exact sequence, an identity-component description or a canonical splitting.','not on the page','The bounded absence is verified; the other-project claim is retained only in its separate table.')
add(272,[81],'idea of the earlier run',list(range(87,133)),'1-1312','','The earlier run cites the Nori/Ayoub degree-zero Hopf-algebra comparison, not disappearance of higher derived structure or existence of a motivic t-structure.','No Nori/Ayoub object is present in the manuscript; comparison belongs to project context.','not on the page','The attribution must remain with the earlier run.')
