def cod(n,folder,scans,lines,kind,words,statement,reconstruction='',check='agrees',reason='Read in the assigned Codex transcription; no NOTES_INDEX verdict is created for a Codex lead.'):
    items.append(dict(id=f'SA06-{n}',sources=[f'codex/{folder}_notes.md; codex/{folder}_transcription.tex'],kind=kind,cote=14,scans=scans,lines=[f'codex/{folder}_transcription.tex:{lines}'],his_words=words,statement=statement,reconstruction=reconstruction,check=check,check_reason=reason))
cod(288,'K14-05',[59,60,61],'3-73','unproved claim','cycles de dimension1; Hom(B_X,A_Y)','A one-cycle on the product of smooth proper varieties defines a homomorphism from the Picard variety of the first to the Albanese variety of the second; normalized divisorial correspondences recover homomorphisms between Albanese/Picard varieties.','Specify rational versus integral coefficients and the variance of the correspondence separately; numerical invariance is a claim about the induced homomorphism, not the full Chow class.')
cod(289,'K14-05',[62,63,64,65],'52-110','self-flagged step','indépendant de l; on peut prendre pour dénominateur','A correspondence induces a rational H¹ isomorphism exactly when its abelian-variety homomorphism is an isogeny. Its inverse is a rational divisor correspondence. The best denominator is queried as the order of the kernel.','The minimal denominator is the exponent needed to annihilate the finite kernel group scheme; its order is only a possible bound. For [m] on an elliptic curve, the two are m and m².')
cod(290,'K14-05',[65,66,67,68],'98-167','unproved claim','transformée de Poincaré; polarisante','An ample correspondence produces an H¹-to-top-cohomology isomorphism, with inverse algebraic over Q. A sufficiently ample complete-intersection curve induces the usual Albanese/Picard polarization up to isogeny.','The exact dimension and twists are retained in the claim registry; no integral inverse is inferred.')
cod(291,'K14-05',[68,69,70],'169-211','unproved claim','cycles de dimension1; inverse','A divisor correspondence inducing a rational H¹ isomorphism has an inverse action induced by a rational one-cycle, by reducing to polarizations and composing correspondences.','The result is rational; denominators and torsion cannot be dropped.')
cod(292,'K14-05',[71],'215-217','self-flagged step','Y-a-t-il tjrs un cycle entier','Two integral inverse-correspondence questions are posed for the Albanese H¹ isomorphism and the Picard/top-cohomology isomorphism; a rational point in a generic symmetric-power fibre is proposed as a sufficient condition for the former.','The two questions are not automatically identical to the integral Hodge conjecture. A modern obstruction or equivalence must be proved for the precise correspondence bidegree.')
cod(293,'K14-05',[73],'222-257','unproved claim','H¹(X,μ_N)≃{}_N Pic(X)','For proper X over a separably closed field and N prime to the characteristic, Kummer theory relates H¹(X,μ_N), Pic⁰[N] and NS[N]; passage to Tate modules yields H¹(X,Zℓ(1))≅TℓPic⁰.','The Picard-scheme identity component can be nonreduced; the prime-to-characteristic Tate module sees its reduced abelian part in the proper normal case.')
cod(294,'K14-05',[73],'239-257','self-flagged step','H^{2n−1}; comp. l-primaire','For smooth proper pure n-dimensional X, duality identifies top-minus-one cohomology modulo its NS-torsion contribution with H¹ of the Picard variety after twist n−1.','The displayed NS[l] with a margin specifying the ℓ-primary component is not merely the subgroup killed by ℓ; finite-coefficient and inverse-limit conventions require checking.')
cod(295,'K14-06',[74],'4-39','self-flagged step','π1(X)^ab; 0?','The Picard/Albanese H¹ and H^{2n−1} comparisons are arranged with abelianized fundamental groups; several endpoint injectivity or surjectivity marks are queried.','A simultaneous exact integral statement needs prime-to-characteristic completions and the NS torsion term; the page is not a fully specified theorem.')
cod(296,'K14-06',[75],'46-70','unproved claim','F(X,Y)=X+Y+λXY','A polynomial binary law over a field with two-sided unit0 and associativity has degree1 in each variable, hence the form X+Y+λXY. The additional polynomial-antipode condition forces λ=0.','The page proves the degree reduction but stops at Consequently before the antipode conclusion; the last sentence is this run’s completion, not text.')
cod(297,'K14-06',[76,78],'75-124;181-234','unproved claim','H¹ est un foncteur additif fidèle; H*=ΛH¹','Abelian varieties form an additive category, duality reverses arrows, first ℓ-adic cohomology is additive and faithful, and the cohomology algebra is the exterior algebra of H¹.','Integral faithfulness is for actual homomorphisms over the specified base; arbitrary Galois-equivariant linear maps require separate arithmetic hypotheses.')
cod(298,'K14-06',[76,78],'80-124;204-234','reading question','Hom(A,A*)^alt; attention au signe','The correspondence between divisors, self-dual homomorphisms and alternating pairings involves a transpose convention and a graded-commutativity sign; pullback, cup product and Pontryagin product use different variance.','The modern Rosati-symmetric homomorphism attached to a line bundle yields an alternating Tate-module pairing; the symbols symmetric and alternating cannot be exchanged without specifying the duality identification.')
cod(299,'K14-06',[80,81,83],'289-350;395-427','unproved claim','u_*1; deg u; Λ^{2n−i}u','Pushforward for a homomorphism A→A′ shifts cohomological degree by2(dim A′−dim A), is dual to pullback in complementary degree, and sends1 to degree times the image class when generically finite.','The page switches the source/target convention and one displayed exterior exponent is ambiguous; dimensions and twists fix the typed modern formula.')
cod(300,'K14-06',[81,85],'333-350;478-487','self-flagged step','déterminer Im u; degré','A nonzero decomposable top wedge determines the rational image subspace and determinant content, but not the integral image lattice.','The full degree cannot be recovered from one ℓ-adic lattice index; that sees only the ℓ-primary factor. The two lattices ℓZe₁+Ze₂ and Ze₁+ℓZe₂ give the same top wedge but are different.')
cod(301,'K14-06',[82,84],'357-385;436-468','unproved claim','C-acyclique; cofinal','Site-specific acyclicity can be tested on Čech complexes of covers and is preserved under a continuous functor only with the stated cofinality and fibre-product compatibility hypotheses.','These site hypotheses matter; arbitrary continuous inverse-image functors need not preserve such acyclicity.')
cod(302,'K14-06',[77,86],'131-170;494-529','unproved claim','H^q(S,F); faisceau abélien sous-jacent','Cohomology of a sheaf of modules agrees with cohomology of its underlying abelian sheaf. The proof uses universal effaceable delta functors and local effacement.','Do not replace this argument by an unsupported claim that the forgetful functor preserves every injective module sheaf.')
